  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). Reporter: Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, mei.chen@brightline.example). Reports leaving work laptop in an Uber last night; does not remember whether it was locked. Device: BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). check_device_status shows it ONLINE right now, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:30:41Z (09:30 Chicago), no warnings \u2014 someone may have it powered on and connected. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 successful sign-ins, all Chicago, Duo push, normal hours; latest 2026-10-08 13:23Z VPN from residential IP 198.51.100.29. No failures or foreign/hosting sign-ins yet. Data exposure: Operations/logistics analyst \u2014 likely M365 mail/files, VPN access with cached sessions. Action taken: block_sign_in queued for technician approval (not yet applied). Needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 while it is online, approve sign-in block, revoke sessions, then password reset once user verified by phone. Asked user for when/where last seen and to file police report / contact Uber lost & found. Side note: user's mailbox is at 99.4% quota.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation always for remote lock/wipe; ticket is P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for letting us know so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. To protect your account, we've asked a technician to block sign-ins to your account for now. Once they approve it, any saved logins on the laptop will stop working, and you won't be able to sign in on other devices until we finish securing things. We've also handed your case to our senior team so they can remotely lock or wipe the laptop if needed. After that, we'll call you to confirm it's you and set a new password. To help us, could you please reply with: (1) roughly what time and where your Uber trip ended, and (2) anything you remember about whether the laptop was asleep, shut, or locked? Please also report the lost item to Uber through the app. If you think it was stolen, please file a police report too. If you get the laptop back, tell us right away.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 P1. User 9 Mei Chen, device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). Device is ONLINE now, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:30:41Z (09:30 CT), no warnings. That means someone may have it powered on. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days look clean: all Chicago, Duo push, normal hours. Last sign-in was 2026-10-08 13:23Z VPN from residential IP 198.51.100.29. No failed or unusual sign-ins. I queued block_sign_in (approval_id 1) because the lock status is unknown. It has not run yet. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) for remote lock/wipe while the device is online, and to revoke sessions. Plan a password reset by phone once the user is verified. Asked the user when and where the laptop was last seen, plus Uber lost item and police report details. Side note: mailbox is at 99.4% of quota.",
